# Never commit backend secrets.
#
# The Supabase ANON key IS committed, deliberately - it is designed to be
# embedded in clients, carries the `anon` role, and grants nothing because every
# table has Row Level Security enabled. See SupabaseConfig.cs.
#
# A service_role key is the opposite: it bypasses RLS entirely. It must never be
# committed, and SupabaseManager refuses to start if it finds one.
.env
.env.*
**/service_role*
**/supabase_secret*

